(i) For a homogeneous, single-phase, liquid having a viscosity less than 45 S.U.S. at 38 °C (100 °F) that does not form a surface film while under test, one of the following test procedures shall be used:
(A) Standard Method of Test for Flash Point by Tag Closed Cup Tester, (ASTM D 56) (IBR;
(B) Standard Test Methods for Flash Point of Liquids by Small Scale Closed-Cup Apparatus, (ASTM D 3278) (IBR;
(C) Standard Test Methods for Flash Point by Small Scale Closed Tester, (ASTM D 3828) (IBR;

(ii) For a liquid other than one meeting all the criteria of paragraph (c)(1)(i) of this section, one of the following test procedures must be used:
(A) Standard Test Methods for Flash Point by Pensky-Martens Closed Cup Tester, (ASTM D 93) (IBR;
(B) Standard Test Methods for Flash Point of Liquids by Small Scale Closed-Cup Apparatus (ASTM D 3278) (IBR;
(C) Determination of Flash/No Flash—Closed Cup Equilibrium Method (ISO 1516) (IBR;
(D) Determination of Flash point—Closed Cup Equilibrium Method (ISO 1523) (IBR;
(E) Determination of Flash Point—Pensky-Martens Closed Cup Method (ISO 2719) (IBR;
